    card title Hobbies

A: What do you do for fun, and how do you say it in Russian? Tom asks Masha; let's listen.
    draw masha masha_name tom tom_name

    draw talk

A: Word for word: what do you love to do? Лю́бишь from lesson twenty-four, and де́лать, to do.
    highlight talk_1_words effect underline color #8f887c part лю́бишь

    draw talk

B: Му́зыка is music, игра́ю is I play, and гита́ра is the guitar.
    highlight talk_2_words effect underline color #8f887c part игра́ю

    draw talk

A: We both play with на: на гита́ре, на пиани́но.
    highlight talk_3_words effect underline color #8f887c part ^на$

    erase talk

    draw talk2

    draw talk2

    draw talk2

A: But sport comes with в: в футбо́л,
    highlight talk2_1_words effect underline color #8f887c part ^в$

A: в те́ннис. Two kinds of play, a little word for each. First, the verb.
    highlight talk2_2_words effect underline color #8f887c part ^в$

    erase talk2

    hide masha masha_name tom tom_name

A: Игра́ть, to play, goes just like чита́ть from lesson twenty-two.
    draw b_ball b_guitar b_lbl

    move b_ball b_guitar b_lbl by [290,0] duration 0.6

A: Я игра́ю, ты игра́ешь, он игра́ет, мы игра́ем, вы игра́ете, они́ игра́ют.
    draw v1 v2 v3 v4 v5 v6

    hide v1 v6

B: Keep игра́ and add the endings you know: ю for я, ют for они́,
    draw cv1 cv6

    hide v2 v3 v4 v5

B: and endings with е for all the rest.
    draw cv2 cv3 cv4 cv5

    erase verb

    draw h_game

A: A game takes в: я игра́ю в футбо́л.
    draw c_ball c_foot

B: And в те́ннис.
    draw c_tennis c_ten

A: Both are he-words, so they stay as they are, like в парк in lesson twenty-seven.
    highlight c_foot c_ten effect underline color #8f887c

    draw h_inst

A: An instrument takes на, and the place ending: гита́ра becomes на гита́ре, as шко́ла became в шко́ле.
    draw c_guitar c_git0 c_git

B: And пиани́но stays as it is: на пиани́но.
    draw c_piano c_pia

B: It's a borrowed word, like кино́ and ко́фе, and those never change.
    draw c_kino

A: So the little word tells you the kind of play: в for a game, на for an instrument. A hook: you play a tune on the piano, and на means on.
    highlight h_game h_inst effect underline color #8f887c

    hide boardC

B: Back to Tom's question: что ты лю́бишь де́лать?
    draw d_q

A: After люблю́, a second verb come (@draw d_books d_1@)s straight from the dictionary, as after бу́ду and могу́: я люблю́ чита́ть.

B: With a verb after it, люблю́ often just means I like: I like reading.
    highlight d_1 effect underline color #8f887c part чита́ть

A: And with our new verb: я люблю́ игра́ть в те́ннис.
    draw d_tennis d_2

B: Слу́шать is to listen: я люблю́ слу́шать му́зыку, with the object ending у, as in люблю́ ма́му.
    draw d_phones d_3

    hide boardD

    quiz "Tom plays the piano: Я игра́ю ___ пиани́но. Which little word?" reveal.text "Я игра́ю на пиани́но." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 290 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        intro: Five questions now, then your score.
        right: На: an instrument takes на.
        wrong: Is the piano a game, or an instrument?
        * в
        + на

    erase question_1_stamp

    ask "Masha plays the guitar. Type the missing word: Я игра́ю на ___." answer ["гитаре"] reveal.text "Я игра́ю на гита́ре." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 290 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        keys: АБВГДЕЁЖЗИЙКЛМНОПРСТУФХЦЧШЩЪЫЬЭЮЯ
        right: Гита́ре: after на, the а of гита́ра makes way for е.
        wrong: Start from гита́ра; with на, what does its а become?

    erase question_2_stamp

    quiz "Mum and dad play tennis: Ма́ма и па́па ___ в те́ннис. Which form fills the gap?" reveal.text "Они́ игра́ют в те́ннис." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 290 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: Mum and dad are они́, so the ending is ют.
        wrong: Mum and dad are они́: which ending goes with они́?
        * игра́ет
        * игра́ем
        + игра́ют

    erase question_3_stamp

    quiz "Which one says I like reading?" reveal.text "Я люблю́ чита́ть." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 290 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice a test t1
        right: After люблю́, the second verb is the dictionary form: чита́ть.
        wrong: After люблю́, which form does the second verb take?
        + Я люблю́ чита́ть.
        * Я люблю́ чита́ю.
        * Мне люблю́ чита́ть.

    erase question_4_stamp

    quiz "Masha's brother plays football: Брат игра́ет ___. Which is right?" reveal.text "Брат игра́ет в футбо́л." reveal.at.x 500 reveal.at.y 290 reveal.style label reveal.size 60 reveal.color #3d3833 voice b test t1
        right: В футбо́л: a game takes в, and a he-word stays as it is.
        wrong: Football is a game, not an instrument; and after в, does a game change?
        * в футбо́ле
        + в футбо́л
        * на футбо́ле

    erase question_5_stamp

    group recap members ["r1","r2","r3","r4"]
    parallel true

A: You got {t1.score} of {t1.total}.
    results test t1 retry true pass 4

    erase recap

    show boardC

A: So to say what you like to do, it's люблю́ and a verb; and to play, в and the game as it is, or на and the instrument.
    highlight h_game h_inst effect underline color #8f887c

    hide boardC

B: А ты? Что ты лю́бишь де́лать? Next time, you'll tell us about yourself. Пока́!
